     "result_text_tail": "d also leave cumulative US cash at \u2013$9.6M in 2030.\n\n**The retail-led route (Option B):** it fails every financial test on the planning team's own numbers. It goes $20.8M below zero (breaking the $18M cap), never pays back by 2030, and cuts group margin to 4.5% in 2027. Its key inputs aren't supported by the evidence:\n- Its sales rate of 4.5 units per store per week is what brands with over 20% awareness achieve; Onsoo is at 4%.\n- Its 30% Amazon boost from retail rests on a correlation that likely runs the other way, since retailers add brands that already sell.\n\nWith more realistic inputs, Option B loses about $31M by 2030.\n\n**Decisions the deck asks the board for:**\n1. Approve Option A with a $5M limit on cumulative US cash outflow.\n2. Restate the targets: $25M+ US revenue in 2030 and $40M by about 2032.\n3. Reject the retail-first route and replace the 2029 retail trigger with stricter evidence gates.\n4. Bring the Japan scale-up to the 2028 plan.\n\n**Choices I made without asking** (all listed on appendix slide A1):\n- I read \"on the way to $40M by 2030\" as $40M of US revenue in 2030, the stricter reading.\n- I read the bandwidth limit as applying to 2027 only.\n- One-time costs count against group margin in the year they're spent, which is conservative.\n- No tax.\n- The years after 2030 are my own projections at 10\u201320% growth a year, flagged wherever they appear.\n\nThe charts are drawn as shapes rather than PowerPoint chart objects, so they look exact but can't be edited as data."
    }
